    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\n`except*` (new in 3.3.0) works in a normal function, but in `async def`, generators, at module level and in module-level class bodies, Cython generates C that uses `__pyx_skip_add_traceback` without declaring it. Cython itself reports no error; the C compiler fails:\n\n```\nerror: '__pyx_skip_add_traceback' undeclared (first use in this function); did you mean '__Pyx_AddTraceback'?\n```\n\n| `except*` inside | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `def` | compiles and works |\n| `async def` | C compile error |\n| generator (`def` with `yield`) | C compile error |\n| async generator | C compile error |\n| module level | C compile error |\n| class body (at module level) | C compile error |\n| class body inside a `def` | compiles and works |\n\n`FuncDefNode.generate_function_definitions` declares the variable. `GeneratorBodyDefNode` overrides that method without the declaration, and the module init function doesn't declare it either.\n\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n`t.py`:\n\n```python\nasync def f():\n    try:\n        raise ExceptionGroup(\"g\", [ValueError()])\n    except* ValueError:\n        r = \"caught\"\n    return r\n```\n\n```\ncython -3 t.py -o t.c\ngcc -O2 -shared -fPIC $(python3-config --includes) t.c -o t$(python3-config --extension-suffix)\n```\n\n`cython` succeeds and `gcc` fails with the error above. Changing `async def` to `def` (and calling it normally) compiles and works.\n\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nThe module compiles, and `asyncio.run(t.f())` returns `\"caught\"`, the same as pure Python.\n\n\n### OS\n\nUbuntu 24.04, x86_64, gcc 13.3\n\n### Python version\n\n3.12.3\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0 (master's Nodes.py still only declares the variable in FuncDefNode)\n\n### Additional context\n\nDeclaring the variable in `GeneratorBodyDefNode` the same way `FuncDefNode` does fixes `async def`, generators and async generators. This is the change I tested:\n\n```diff\n--- a/Cython/Compiler/Nodes.py\n+++ b/Cython/Compiler/Nodes.py\n@@ -5005,6 +5005,9 @@\n \n             for cname, type in code.funcstate.all_managed_temps():\n                 code.put_xdecref(cname, type)\n+            if code.funcstate.has_except_star:\n+                tempvardecl_code.putln(\n+                    f\"int {Naming.skip_add_traceback_cname} = 0;\")\n             code.putln(\"if (__Pyx_PyErr_Occurred()) {\")  # we allow exit without GeneratorExit / StopIteration\n             if tracing:\n                 code.put_trace_exception_propagating()\n```\n\n`except*` at module level, or in a module-level class body, still fails with this change. Those cases need the same declaration in the module init function.\n",
